# SAMPLE-MIRRORDIR — template for the build-pdfs output mirror
#
# To use: copy this file to .MIRRORDIR at the repo top level (or in any directory
# whose subtree you want mirrored elsewhere -- the nearest .MIRRORDIR above a build
# directory wins). build-pdfs then mirrors every PDF it builds under that
# directory into the base named below, preserving the path relative to the
# .MIRRORDIR's own directory: a source in REPO/integrals/lectures ships to
# BASE/integrals/lectures. Missing mirror sub-directories are created; the base
# itself must already exist (else build-pdfs warns and builds locally).
#
# Format:
#   - One bare line is the mirror base directory; a leading ~ is expanded.
#   - Optionally add a line reading BOTH to build locally AND copy the PDFs to
#     the mirror, keeping both. Without it the build goes straight to the mirror,
#     with no local copy. (COPY, the songsheets synonym, is NOT recognised here
#     -- build-pdfs deliberately doesn't wire it yet.)
#   - `LABEL: path' lines name extra flat destinations (see below).
#   - Blank lines and #-comment lines (like these) are ignored; the base path and
#     the BOTH keyword may appear in any order.
#
# Named destinations:
#   A `LABEL: path' line here gives a directory a NAME. A source asks for a PDF
#   to be dropped there, flat and IN ADDITION to the mirror, with a `%! copies:'
#   magic comment naming that label -- e.g.
#
#       %! copies: default-->TA-dir, instructor-->TA-dir(from 2026-10-01)
#
#   where `default' is the base (student) PDF and the other names are views from
#   the source's own `%! views:' line. The labelled directory must already exist;
#   a missing label or directory warns and skips only that extra copy.
#
#   This file is only the ADDRESS BOOK. Which document goes where is stated in
#   the source, which is what keeps machine-specific paths out of the git-tracked
#   .tex -- and a `(from YYYY-MM-DD)' embargo, which holds a copy until that date
#   arrives, is likewise the source's business, not this file's.
#
# .MIRRORDIR is meant to be git-ignored, so each machine or checkout can point
# somewhere different (keep SAMPLE-MIRRORDIR tracked as the reference).
#
# Edit and uncomment the lines you want (drop the leading "# ").

# ~/Documents/2teach/course-COPY
# BOTH
# TA-dir: ~/shared/calc-ta
